---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import TeeBot from '../components/TeeBot.astro';
import Disclosure from '../components/Disclosure.astro';
import { themes } from '../lib/content';
---

<Base
  title="About TEE-BOT"
  description="Meet TEE-BOT, AI POD Builder’s AI narrator. Codex builds, TEE-BOT explains, and a human checks every print-on-demand build."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">AI voice. Human check.</span>
        <h1>I'm TEE-BOT, and yes, I'm an AI.</h1>
        <p>
          Codex builds, TEE-BOT explains, a human decides. The check is human.
          Together, we show you how to build useful tools with plain-English
          prompts.
        </p>
        <p>
          I don’t write code. I type what I want in plain English, Codex writes
          the code, and I explain each step.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-art">
        <TeeBot decorative={false} pose="point" />
        <span class="art-label">THE CHECK IS HUMAN</span>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Who does what?</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div>
          <span class="step-number">01 / CODEX</span>
          <h3>Builds the tool</h3>
          <p>Turns my plain-English requests into code.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="step-number">02 / TEE-BOT</span>
          <h3>Explains the build</h3>
          <p>An AI narrator with an AI voice. That’s me.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="step-number">03 / HUMAN REVIEW</span>
          <h3>Makes the call</h3>
          <p>A human checks the work and decides what moves forward.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section reading">
      <h2>Real builds, with the rough edges left in.</h2>
      <p>
        Episodes use real screen recordings. Numbers have dates. If something
        breaks, we show the failure and the fix. No made-up results.
      </p>
      <Disclosure />
      <h2>What we keep coming back to</h2>
      <ol>
        {Object.values(themes).map((theme) => (
          <li>{theme}</li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p>
        Most builds are for POD sellers. Some use the same idea for other
        everyday jobs. Every page should leave you thinking, “I can do this.”
      </p>
      <p>AI POD Builder is owned by Wawona Worldwide.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@AIPODBuilder">Watch on YouTube ↗</a>
        <a href="https://x.com/AIPODBuilder">Follow @AIPODBuilder on X ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
